#: doc/classes/TileMapLayer.xml
msgid ""
"Node for 2D tile-based maps. A [TileMapLayer] uses a [TileSet] which contain "
"a list of tiles which are used to create grid-based maps. Unlike the "
"[TileMap] node, which is deprecated, [TileMapLayer] has only one layer of "
"tiles. You can use several [TileMapLayer] to achieve the same result as a "
"[TileMap] node.\n"
"For performance reasons, all TileMap updates are batched at the end of a "
"frame. Notably, this means that scene tiles from a "
"[TileSetScenesCollectionSource] are initialized after their parent. This is "
"only queued when inside the scene tree.\n"
"To force an update earlier on, call [method update_internals].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For performance and compatibility reasons, the coordinates "
"serialized by [TileMapLayer] are limited to 16-bit signed integers, i.e. the "
"range for X and Y coordinates is from [code]-32768[/code] to [code]32767[/"
"code]. When saving tile data, tiles outside this range are wrapped."
msgstr ""

